# Allowed differences between Air.interp and the old opcode.fold
# (tests/differential/air.zig, `zig build diff-air`).
# One line: <opcode> <kind> [<ulps>] <reason>. Kinds: declines (the fold has
# no value, the interpreter has one), ulp N (both real, at most N ulps
# apart), wide (both integer, an operand past 32 bits). A line whose kind
# never occurs over the sweep fails the run.
#
# The ulp bounds are the sum of the two implementations' documented
# accuracies, rounded up: the fold calls lib/contract/gm.zig (VerA's own
# exp/log/pow, the sin/cos quotient for tan; VD-123), the interpreter
# std.math and the Zig builtins. Measured at seed 0xA12F01D: exp 1, pow 1,
# tan 2, log10 1.
exp ulp 2 gm.exp (<= 0.52 ulp, fma-free) against @exp (< 1 ulp)
pow ulp 2 gm.pow (<= 0.54 ulp) against interp's f128 exp(y ln|x|) rounded once (<= 0.5 ulp)
tan ulp 3 gm.tan is sin(x)/cos(x) (<= 2 ulp, VD-123) against @tan (< 1 ulp)
log10 ulp 3 a subnormal: interp scales it by 2^54 and subtracts 54 log10(2) (two roundings, <= 1.5 ulp) because @log10 is off there; gm.log10 <= 0.67 ulp
